{
  "findings": [
    "Under the uniform weak-composition law conditioned only on S_R=K, let Z_{R,K}=binom(K+R-1,R-1) and define Phi_n(u)=binom(u+n-1,n-1) for n>=1, Phi_0(u)=1_{u=0}, with Phi_n(u)=0 for u<0. For a block beginning after j pairs, of length L, and word b=(b_1,...,b_L) in {1,...,B_0}^L, exact counting gives P(C_q | S_R=K)=Z_{R,K}^{-1} sum_{h>=0} sum_b Phi_{2j}(h) prod_l(b_l+1) 1_{C_q(h,b)} Phi_{R-2j-2L}(K-h-|b|). The factor prod_l(b_l+1) counts the two raw-coordinate splits of each pair total. This includes both parity cases and all boundary conventions.",
    "If the marker depends only on w=|b|, the inner word sum reduces to a_L(w)=[x^w](sum_{b=1}^{B_0}(b+1)x^b)^L. The same identity applies to G_q intersect resonance or to C_q by inserting the corresponding indicator. It is an exact one-block coefficient identity, not an independence statement.",
    "The identity does not control E[exp(-lambda sum_q 1_{C_q})]. That quantity requires joint counts for several disjoint blocks, including the evolving prefix total h and the arithmetic low/nonresonance indicators. Neither the displayed coefficient formula nor exchangeability supplies those joint bounds.",
    "A sufficient narrower missing estimate is the following local hazard statement. There should exist p_*>0 and, for every sufficiently large actual array, a deterministic ordered subgrid of n_R=ceil(log R / -log rho) disjoint blocks, where rho=1-p_*(1-exp(-lambda))<1, such that for every admissible revealed history H_i before block i, P(C_{q_i} | H_i, S_R=K, exact first-passage data) >= p_* for i=1,...,n_R. Iterated conditioning would then give E[exp(-lambda sum_q 1_{C_q})] <= rho^{n_R} <= 1/R. This asks only for O(log R) blocks rather than the full global estimate, but it is not established; low entry phases and positive amplified resonances prevent deriving the hazard from the coefficient identity alone."
  ],
  "claim_status": {
    "status": "OPEN",
    "reason": "No rigorous proof or actual accessible counterexample was obtained. The exact composition count is established under conditioning on S_R=K, but the marked joint-occupation/Laplace estimate remains unproved."
  },
  "first_missing_step": {
    "statement": "Prove the uniform conditional marked-block hazard inequality in the findings, with quantifiers uniform over all sufficiently large actual coupled arrays and all histories of positive conditional probability.",
    "why_it_is_missing": "The required lower bound must simultaneously exclude low entry states and exact positive amplified resonances. The supplied marginal coefficient identities count words but provide no uniform arithmetic or joint-history bound for those exclusions."
  },
  "unexpected_findings": [
    "Escalation candidate: the coefficient identity above is directly valid for the uniform law conditioned on S_R=K. If 'exact first-passage data' imposes any additional restriction beyond that restarted composition law, its conditional numerator and denominator must be rederived; exchangeability alone does not justify using the same ratio."
  ]
}
